### 3.7 Signal of \(D^{0}\)-Meson.

The \(D^{0}\) meson signal was obtained in this analysis by using the full production of run14 SL16id library. The event selection cuts, tracks quality cuts, and the topological TMVA cuts were applied to select the \(D^{0}\) candidates. The significance of the \(D^{0}\) candidates peak is defined as the ratio of signal to background \(S/\sqrt{S+B}\) (with \(S\) denoting a signal which is fit by the Gaussian function and \(B\) denoting the subtracted background which is fit by the 3rd order polynomial function). The resulting signal and background are fitted across the mass range of 1.73 to 2.00 GeV/\(c\), and when computing the significance, the ratio is taken over a mass range that corresponds to \(3\sigma\) on either side of the mass peak.

