Table 4.1: Selection cuts of tracks for event plane calculationFigure 4.1: \(\Psi_{2}\) Event plane before recentering (upper panel) and \(\Psi_{2}\) Event plane after recentering (lower panel)

the resolution to estimate the \(\Psi_{2}\).

\[v_{2}=\frac{v_{2}^{\rm obs}}{R_{\Psi}}=\frac{v_{2}^{\rm obs}}{\langle\cos 2(\Psi_{2 }-\Psi_{r})\rangle} \tag{4.7}\]

The resolution equation can be solved analytically as [76]:

\[\langle\cos 2(\Psi_{2}-\Psi_{r})\rangle=\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2\sqrt{2}}\chi_{2}\exp(- \chi_{2}^{2}/4)[I_{0}(\chi_{2}^{2}/4)+I_{1}(\chi_{2}^{2}/4)] \tag{4.8}\]

where \(I_{0}\) is the modified Bessel functions.

\[\chi_{2}=\frac{v_{2}}{\sigma}\quad and\quad\sigma^{2}=\frac{\langle w^{2} \rangle}{2N\langle w\rangle^{2}} \tag{4.9}\]

Figure 4.2 shows the resolution for the second harmonic event plane as function of centrality.

